<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Product shell for dist/wds-win-x86_64.msi.
  File components are harvested at packaging time via wixl-heat, then
  scripts/win-msi-harvest.py pins wds_editor.exe + private DLLs under INSTALLDIR.
  Config is NOT installed: runtime writes %LOCALAPPDATA%\WDS\config\config.yml.
  UI: scripts/win-msi-ui.wxs (install dir + shortcuts + progress + exit).

  Language must stay 1033 to match wixl Template summary (x64;1033).

  dest rebuilds are a major upgrade: Product Id='*' (new ProductCode each
  package), ProductVersion stays 1.0.0, UpgradeCode is fixed. Double-clicking
  a newer MSI finds the previous ProductCode via Upgrade and
  RemoveExistingProducts replaces it. INSTALLDIR is adopted from the
  remembered HKLM path; ARP still shows one entry.

  A fixed ProductCode cannot do that. Same ProductCode + a new PackageCode
  (wixl always rewrites Revision Number) is a small update. msiexec rejects
  that with 1638 / "another version of this product is already installed"
  BEFORE any sequence runs, so SetReinstallAll / UpdateDlg / REINSTALL inside
  the package never get a chance. Command-line REINSTALL=ALL is the only
  in-package-identity workaround, and dest users double-click the MSI.

  Do not use MajorUpgrade: its downgrade LaunchCondition
  (NOT WIX_DOWNGRADE_DETECTED) also surfaces as 1638 when ProductVersion is
  pinned at 1.0.0. A single Upgrade row from 0.0.0 with no VersionMax is
  enough. FindRelatedProducts skips the ProductCode being installed, so the
  same .msi file still opens as maintenance / repair.

  Because ProductVersion is pinned, ordering has to come from somewhere else:
  the numeric build stamp. InstallStamp writes WDS_BUILD_TS (seconds since
  2020-01-01Z, i.e. `date -u +%s - 1577836800`) to
  HKLM\Software\WDS\Editor\BuildTs, and AppSearch reads it back into
  WDS_INSTALLED_TS. It must stay inside the signed 32-bit range msiexec compares
  in, which is the only reason it is not a raw Unix timestamp. A companion
  BuildId string holds <sha>-<UTC time> for diagnostics; no condition reads it.

  Three outcomes, all decided before costing:
    - WDS_INSTALLED_TS =  WDS_BUILD_TS and Installed -> the SAME MSI again:
      REPAIR (REINSTALL=ALL + REINSTALLMODE=ecmus, the stock repair mode).
    - another ProductCode with this UpgradeCode, or a different stamp ->
      UPDATE: FindRelatedProducts lists the old product; RemoveExistingProducts
      uninstalls it; this package installs into the remembered folder.
    - WDS_INSTALLED_TS >  WDS_BUILD_TS -> that build is NEWER: the
      LaunchCondition refuses the install. WDS_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE=1 overrides it.
  msiexec exposes no property for the installed package code, which is why a
  stamp of our own is needed at all.

  ProductCode and the component GUIDs are a MATCHED PAIR - never change one
  without the other:
    - This per-build ProductCode requires per-build component GUIDs.
      win-msi-harvest.py derives them with UUID5 from WDS_BUILD_TS plus the
      install-relative path (authored components use the same salt + Id),
      and package-target.sh rejects Guid='*' on the payload component.
    - Mixing a fresh ProductCode with path-stable / shared GUIDs makes two
      different products claim the same component: costing treats it as
      already installed and skips InstallFiles, then the old product's
      uninstall deletes the files it skipped. That combination is what
      224cdbd and 67c5dd8 were fighting; do not recreate it.

  RemoveExistingProducts sits immediately after InstallInitialize ("after
  InstallInitialize and before any actions that generate execution script",
  one of the four placements the action documents). It removes the previous
  dest / leftover Id='*' / main product, whose component GUIDs are NOT this
  package's, so that uninstall cannot delete files this build writes; the
  removal is also inside the transaction, so a later failure can roll it
  back. Never sequence it next to InstallFiles or InstallFinalize-after-
  file-actions: msiexec rejects the mid-script placement with error 2613.

  Shortcuts are MSI Shortcut table entries (Advertise=no + Target=exe).
  wixl defaults Advertise=yes; the Target path keeps them non-advertised.
  CREATE_* + Component.Condition chooses which .lnk files exist. wixl 0.103
  crashes on <Component><Condition> (added in 0.106); package-target.sh
  writes those Condition columns after wixl. ShortcutPrefs writes the
  checkbox state to HKLM on every install (first run and every dest
  upgrade). AppSearch reads it back into CREATE_* only if those
  properties are empty: a Property-table default of 1 would block the
  overlay, so the default is a Type 51 CA that runs only when the
  search found nothing. Desktop/Start Menu components are Transitive so
  CREATE_* is re-evaluated on a later rebuild, not only the first.

  InstallDirDlg uses Edit (not PathEdit). PathEdit on a not-yet-created
  INSTALLDIR can clear the property; Edit plus InitWdsInstallDir keeps it.
  First-install WDS_INSTALLDIR is applied BEFORE CostInitialize. Updates
  never retarget the directory.

  Repair/update rewrite files (REINSTALLMODE ecmus/vamus) and msiexec stages
  rollback copies as <volume>\Config.Msi\*.rbf. The default ROOTDRIVE is the
  local volume with the most free space, often a data drive such as D:\ whose
  root ACL does not let SYSTEM set file security. Error 1926 / Error 5 on
  D:\Config.Msi\*.rbf is that failure. SetRootDrive pins ROOTDRIVE to
  WindowsVolume before CostInitialize so rollback stays on the OS volume.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Product Id="*"
           Name="WDS Editor"
           Language="1033"
           Version="$(var.ProductVersion)"
           Manufacturer="WDS"
           UpgradeCode="A7E3C2B1-9F4D-4E8A-9C6B-1D2E3F4A5B6C">
    <Package InstallerVersion="500"
             Compressed="yes"
             InstallScope="perMachine"
             Description="WDS Chart Editor (Windows x64)"
             Comments="Self-contained editor; preferences live under LocalAppData"/>

    <!-- Any other ProductCode with this UpgradeCode (previous dest rebuilds,
         the old fixed 8BEDBB5B-... identity, leftover Id='*' / main builds)
         is uninstalled. The current ProductCode is skipped by
         FindRelatedProducts. wixl 0.103 cannot author VersionMin and
         VersionMax both empty, so Minimum starts at 0.0.0. -->
    <Upgrade Id="A7E3C2B1-9F4D-4E8A-9C6B-1D2E3F4A5B6C">
      <UpgradeVersion Property="WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED"
                      Minimum="0.0.0"
                      IncludeMinimum="yes"
                      MigrateFeatures="yes"/>
    </Upgrade>
    <!-- ProductVersion is pinned, so ordering between dest builds is the
         build stamp, not MajorUpgrade. "&lt;=" is escaped XML. -->
    <Condition Message="A newer build of WDS Editor is already installed (build [WDS_INSTALLED_ID]). Uninstall it first, or pass WDS_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE=1 to install this older build anyway.">NOT Installed OR NOT WDS_INSTALLED_TS OR WDS_INSTALLED_TS &lt;= WDS_BUILD_TS OR WDS_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE</Condition>
    <MediaTemplate EmbedCab="yes"/>

    <Property Id="ARPPRODUCTICON" Value="WdsEditorIcon"/>
    <!-- Overwrite mode for a normal install (no prior product, or a legacy
         Id='*' product that RemoveExistingProducts already removed): force every
         file, rewrite machine and user registry, reinstall shortcuts. The
         recache flag 'v' is deliberately NOT here - msiexec forbids it on a
         first installation - and the Installed-only actions below override this
         value: repair for the same build, vamus for a different build. -->
    <Property Id="REINSTALLMODE" Value="amus"/>
    <!-- CREATE_* are yes/no. msiexec treats a property value of 0 as unset,
         so never write 0. AppSearch must NOT write CREATE_*. Search into
         WDS_SAVED_* instead. Registry writes are yes/no. A leftover "1" is
         still treated as on; a leftover "0" or empty plus a prior install
         is treated as off. -->
    <Property Id="CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT" Secure="yes"/>
    <Property Id="CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT" Secure="yes"/>
    <Property Id="WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindDesktopPref"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="CreateDesktopShortcut"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="yes"/>
    </Property>
    <Property Id="WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindStartMenuPref"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="CreateStartMenuShortcut"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="yes"/>
    </Property>
    <Property Id="WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindDesktopPref32"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="CreateDesktopShortcut"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="no"/>
    </Property>
    <Property Id="WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindStartMenuPref32"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="CreateStartMenuShortcut"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="no"/>
    </Property>
    <!-- Parent folder chosen in BrowseDlg; CustomAction appends "\WDS Editor". -->
    <Property Id="WDSINSTALLPARENT" Secure="yes"/>
    <!-- Edit (not PathEdit) binds here. Copied to INSTALLDIR on first-install Next. -->
    <Property Id="WDS_INSTALLDIR" Secure="yes"/>
    <!-- Remembered path from an older Id='*' MSI (Win64 HKLM, 32-bit fallback).
         Same-product updates use the existing Directory table, not this. -->
    <Property Id="WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindWdsInstallDir"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="InstallDir"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="yes"/>
    </Property>
    <Property Id="WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL32" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindWdsInstallDir32"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="InstallDir"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="no"/>
    </Property>
    <!-- Build stamp, injected at package time (wixl -D BuildTs=... -D BuildId=...).
         WDS_BUILD_TS is the one that decides: equal means the same MSI is being
         run again, smaller means the installed build is older, larger means it
         is newer. It counts seconds from 2020-01-01Z to stay inside the signed
         32-bit range msiexec compares in. Every package produced gets a new
         value, even from an unchanged commit, so only the very same .msi file
         can reuse one. WDS_BUILD_ID is diagnostics only. -->
    <Property Id="WDS_BUILD_TS" Value="$(var.BuildTs)" Secure="yes"/>
    <Property Id="WDS_BUILD_ID" Value="$(var.BuildId)" Secure="yes"/>
    <Property Id="WDS_INSTALLED_TS" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindWdsBuildTs"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="BuildTs"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="yes"/>
    </Property>
    <Property Id="WDS_INSTALLED_ID" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="FindWdsBuildId"
                      Root="HKLM"
                      Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                      Name="BuildId"
                      Type="raw"
                      Win64="yes"/>
    </Property>
    <!-- Escape hatch for the downgrade guard, e.g. to go back to an older build
         while bisecting: msiexec /i pkg.msi WDS_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE=1 -->
    <Property Id="WDS_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE" Secure="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetInstallDirFromBrowse"
                  Property="INSTALLDIR"
                  Value="[WDSINSTALLPARENT]\WDS Editor"/>
    <CustomAction Id="AdoptPreviousInstall32"
                  Property="WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL"
                  Value="[WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL32]"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetInstallDirFromPrevious"
                  Property="INSTALLDIR"
                  Value="[WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL]"/>
    <CustomAction Id="InitWdsInstallDir"
                  Property="WDS_INSTALLDIR"
                  Value="[INSTALLDIR]"/>
    <CustomAction Id="ApplyWdsInstallDir"
                  Property="INSTALLDIR"
                  Value="[WDS_INSTALLDIR]"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetArpInstallLocation"
                  Property="ARPINSTALLLOCATION"
                  Value="[INSTALLDIR]"/>
    <!-- Must end with '\'. WindowsVolume is the OS volume (typically C:\).
         Command-line ROOTDRIVE= still wins (NOT ROOTDRIVE). -->
    <CustomAction Id="SetRootDrive"
                  Property="ROOTDRIVE"
                  Value="[WindowsVolume]"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetReinstallAll"
                  Property="REINSTALL"
                  Value="ALL"/>
    <!-- Reinstalling over the SAME build: repair. ecmus is exactly what the
         stock maintenance screen's Repair button publishes (VerifyReadyDlg:
         ReinstallMode=ecmus), so the interactive and silent paths agree:
         missing, corrupt or equal-version files are rewritten plus registry and
         shortcuts, and the package is not re-cached. 'a' is deliberately absent
         - forcing every file is the update path's job. -->
    <CustomAction Id="SetReinstallModeRepair"
                  Property="REINSTALLMODE"
                  Value="ecmus"/>
    <!-- Reinstalling over a DIFFERENT build: update in place. Force every file
         ('a') because a same-version rebuild is invisible to version/checksum
         rules, and re-cache the package ('v') so a later Repair cannot restore
         the previous build out of %WINDIR%\Installer. -->
    <CustomAction Id="SetReinstallModeUpdate"
                  Property="REINSTALLMODE"
                  Value="vamus"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetWdsHadInstall"
                  Property="WDS_HAD_INSTALL"
                  Value="1"/>
    <CustomAction Id="ApplyDesktopOn"
                  Property="CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="ApplyDesktopOff"
                  Property="CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="no"/>
    <CustomAction Id="ApplyStartMenuOn"
                  Property="CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="ApplyStartMenuOff"
                  Property="CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="no"/>
    <CustomAction Id="DefaultDesktopShortcut"
                  Property="CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="DefaultStartMenuShortcut"
                  Property="CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetRegDesktopYes"
                  Property="WDS_REG_DESKTOP"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetRegDesktopNo"
                  Property="WDS_REG_DESKTOP"
                  Value="no"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetRegStartYes"
                  Property="WDS_REG_STARTMENU"
                  Value="yes"/>
    <CustomAction Id="SetRegStartNo"
                  Property="WDS_REG_STARTMENU"
                  Value="no"/>

    <UIRef Id="WdsUI"/>

    <InstallUISequence>
      <!-- After costing so INSTALLDIR is the resolved path (existing product
           or remembered / default). Dialogs are After this action. -->
      <Custom Action="InitWdsInstallDir" After="CostFinalize">
        NOT WDS_INSTALLDIR
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetRootDrive" After="AppSearch" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT ROOTDRIVE
      </Custom>
      <!-- After=AppSearch without Before=CostInitialize is parked after the
           dialogs (wixl 0.103). UpdateDlg then shows the default Program
           Files path, and Execute ApplyWdsInstallDir writes that stale
           WDS_INSTALLDIR over the registry folder. -->
      <Custom Action="AdoptPreviousInstall32" After="SetRootDrive" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL32 AND NOT WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL AND NOT Installed
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetInstallDirFromPrevious" After="AdoptPreviousInstall32" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL AND NOT Installed
      </Custom>
      <!-- Must sit before CostInitialize: wixl otherwise parks After=AppSearch
           extras after the dialogs, and ShortcutsDlg would publish no for an
           unset box before the default yes is applied. Off is "no", never 0. -->
      <Custom Action="SetWdsHadInstall" After="SetInstallDirFromPrevious" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_INSTALLED_TS OR WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyDesktopOn" After="SetWdsHadInstall" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="1" OR WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="yes" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="1" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="yes")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyDesktopOff" After="ApplyDesktopOn" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="0" OR WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="no" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="0" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="no" OR WDS_HAD_INSTALL)
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyStartMenuOn" After="ApplyDesktopOff" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="1" OR WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="yes" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="1" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="yes")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyStartMenuOff" After="ApplyStartMenuOn" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="0" OR WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="no" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="0" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="no" OR WDS_HAD_INSTALL)
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="DefaultDesktopShortcut" After="ApplyStartMenuOff" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="DefaultStartMenuShortcut" After="DefaultDesktopShortcut" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no")
      </Custom>
    </InstallUISequence>
    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <!-- Removes any other ProductCode that FindRelatedProducts listed
           (previous dest, leftover Id='*' dest / main). Skips this exact
           ProductCode, so the same .msi file is still a reinstall.
           Placement is window 2; InstallFiles is error 2613. -->
      <RemoveExistingProducts After="InstallInitialize"/>
      <!-- User-typed / UI path must be applied before costing, not after. -->
      <Custom Action="SetRootDrive" After="AppSearch" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT ROOTDRIVE
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="AdoptPreviousInstall32" After="SetRootDrive" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL32 AND NOT WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL AND NOT Installed
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetInstallDirFromPrevious" After="AdoptPreviousInstall32" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL AND NOT Installed
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetWdsHadInstall" After="SetInstallDirFromPrevious" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_INSTALLED_TS OR WDS_PREVIOUS_INSTALL
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyDesktopOn" After="SetWdsHadInstall" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="1" OR WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="yes" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="1" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="yes")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyDesktopOff" After="ApplyDesktopOn" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="0" OR WDS_SAVED_DESKTOP="no" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="0" OR WDS_DESKTOP_PREF32="no" OR WDS_HAD_INSTALL)
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyStartMenuOn" After="ApplyDesktopOff" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="1" OR WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="yes" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="1" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="yes")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyStartMenuOff" After="ApplyStartMenuOn" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no") AND (WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="0" OR WDS_SAVED_STARTMENU="no" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="0" OR WDS_STARTMENU_PREF32="no" OR WDS_HAD_INSTALL)
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="DefaultDesktopShortcut" After="ApplyStartMenuOff" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="no")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="DefaultStartMenuShortcut" After="DefaultDesktopShortcut" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT (CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes" OR CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="no")
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetRegDesktopYes" After="DefaultStartMenuShortcut" Before="CostInitialize">
        CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes"
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetRegDesktopNo" After="SetRegDesktopYes" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes"
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetRegStartYes" After="SetRegDesktopNo" Before="CostInitialize">
        CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes"
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetRegStartNo" After="SetRegStartYes" Before="CostInitialize">
        NOT CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes"
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="ApplyWdsInstallDir" After="SetInstallDirFromPrevious" Before="CostInitialize">
        WDS_INSTALLDIR AND NOT Installed
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetReinstallAll" After="AppSearch" Before="CostInitialize">
        Installed AND NOT REMOVE AND NOT REINSTALL AND NOT RESUME AND NOT PATCH
      </Custom>
      <!-- Same MSI already installed: WDS_INSTALLED_TS (read by AppSearch)
           equals this package's stamp, so repair instead of overwriting. A
           leftover Id='*' product outranks repair and falls through to update,
           matching the MaintenanceTypeDlg / UpdateDlg split in win-msi-ui.wxs.
           NOT REMOVE keeps this out of the maintenance screen's Remove path. -->
      <Custom Action="SetReinstallModeRepair" After="AppSearch" Before="CostInitialize">
        Installed AND NOT REMOVE AND NOT RESUME AND NOT PATCH AND WDS_INSTALLED_TS = WDS_BUILD_TS AND NOT WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED AND NOT WIX_SAME_VERSION_UPGRADE_DETECTED
      </Custom>
      <!-- An older build, or one that predates the stamp (the property is empty
           then): update in place. No NOT REINSTALL here on purpose - the UI may
           have set REINSTALL already and the mode still has to be normalised
           for this case. A NEWER installed build never reaches this: the
           LaunchCondition above refuses the install first. "&lt;>" is
           msiexec's not-equal operator, escaped because this is XML text. -->
      <Custom Action="SetReinstallModeUpdate" After="AppSearch" Before="CostInitialize">
        Installed AND NOT REMOVE AND NOT RESUME AND NOT PATCH AND (NOT WDS_INSTALLED_TS OR WDS_INSTALLED_TS &lt;> WDS_BUILD_TS)
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="SetArpInstallLocation" After="InstallValidate">
        NOT REMOVE="ALL"
      </Custom>
    </InstallExecuteSequence>

    <Directory Id="TARGETDIR" Name="SourceDir">
      <Directory Id="ProgramFiles64Folder">
        <Directory Id="INSTALLDIR" Name="WDS Editor"/>
      </Directory>
      <Directory Id="ProgramMenuFolder">
        <Directory Id="WdsStartMenuFolder" Name="WDS Editor"/>
      </Directory>
      <Directory Id="DesktopFolder" Name="Desktop"/>
    </Directory>

    <DirectoryRef Id="INSTALLDIR">
      <Component Id="RegistryInstallDir" Guid="$(var.GuidRegistryInstallDir)" Win64="yes">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="InstallDir"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="[INSTALLDIR]"
                       KeyPath="yes"/>
      </Component>
      <!-- MSI-owned prefs (WriteRegistryValues). Written on first install and
           again on every dest upgrade so the last checkbox state is what the
           next package reads. AppSearch + the Default* CAs restore CREATE_*. -->
      <Component Id="ShortcutPrefs" Guid="$(var.GuidShortcutPrefs)" Win64="yes">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="CreateDesktopShortcut"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="[WDS_REG_DESKTOP]"
                       KeyPath="yes"/>
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="CreateStartMenuShortcut"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="[WDS_REG_STARTMENU]"/>
      </Component>
      <!-- Build identity of the installation: BuildTs decides repair / update /
           refuse, BuildId is there so a human can see which commit is
           installed. Per-build GUID, see the header. -->
      <Component Id="InstallStamp" Guid="$(var.GuidInstallStamp)" Win64="yes">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="BuildTs"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="[WDS_BUILD_TS]"
                       KeyPath="yes"/>
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="BuildId"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="[WDS_BUILD_ID]"/>
      </Component>
    </DirectoryRef>

    <!-- Do not author <Condition> here: wixl 0.103 dumps core
         ("unhandled child Component node Condition"). The Condition
         column is set after compile: CREATE_DESKTOP_SHORTCUT="yes". -->
    <DirectoryRef Id="DesktopFolder">
      <Component Id="DesktopShortcut" Guid="$(var.GuidDesktopShortcut)" Win64="yes">
        <Shortcut Id="WdsEditorDesktop"
                  Directory="DesktopFolder"
                  Name="WDS Editor"
                  Description="World Dai Star chart editor"
                  Target="[#WdsFile_wds_editor_exe]"
                  WorkingDirectory="INSTALLDIR"
                  Icon="WdsEditorIcon"
                  Advertise="no"/>
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="DesktopShortcutInstalled"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="1"
                       KeyPath="yes"/>
      </Component>
    </DirectoryRef>

    <!-- Condition column patched after wixl: CREATE_STARTMENU_SHORTCUT="yes". -->
    <DirectoryRef Id="WdsStartMenuFolder">
      <Component Id="StartMenuShortcut" Guid="$(var.GuidStartMenuShortcut)" Win64="yes">
        <Shortcut Id="WdsEditorStartMenu"
                  Directory="WdsStartMenuFolder"
                  Name="WDS Editor"
                  Description="World Dai Star chart editor"
                  Target="[#WdsFile_wds_editor_exe]"
                  WorkingDirectory="INSTALLDIR"
                  Icon="WdsEditorIcon"
                  Advertise="no"/>
        <RemoveFolder Id="RemoveWdsStartMenuFolder" On="uninstall"/>
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM"
                       Key="Software\WDS\Editor"
                       Name="StartMenuShortcutInstalled"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="1"
                       KeyPath="yes"/>
      </Component>
    </DirectoryRef>

    <!-- Prefer BMP-only ICO generated at package time (PNG-compressed ICO can crash msiexec UI). -->
    <Icon Id="WdsEditorIcon" SourceFile="$(var.SourceDir)/wds-msi.ico"/>

    <Feature Id="ProductFeature" Title="WDS Editor" Level="1" AllowAdvertise="no" Absent="disallow">
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="ProductFiles"/>
      <ComponentRef Id="RegistryInstallDir"/>
      <ComponentRef Id="ShortcutPrefs"/>
      <ComponentRef Id="InstallStamp"/>
      <ComponentRef Id="DesktopShortcut"/>
      <ComponentRef Id="StartMenuShortcut"/>
    </Feature>
  </Product>
</Wix>
